# Git LFS tracking.
#
# Why: the repository is 217 MB of tracked files, and 80 % of the .git object
# database is build output that CI regenerates and uploads as an artifact on
# every push (docs/AUDIT_2026-10-21.md §4). `web/index.pck` alone has been
# committed 19 times at ~35 MB each. Tracking these under LFS keeps new commits
# light without rewriting history: the old blobs stay where they are.
#
# What is deliberately NOT tracked: anything the game loads at runtime from a
# normal clone (`game/assets/**`, fonts, the .ogv videos, .gd/.tscn/.py).
# Those are 6 MB of GLB, 1.4 MB of fonts and 1.7 MB of video — moving them to
# LFS would make a plain `git clone` produce a project that will not run
# without git-lfs installed, which is a worse handover than 9 MB of history.
#
# Setup on a machine that has git-lfs:
#     scripts/setup_lfs.sh            # verify + track (no history rewrite)
#     scripts/setup_lfs.sh --migrate  # rewrite history (destructive, off by default)

# Third-party archives (already LFS before this pass).
*.zip filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# The web export templates are NOT under LFS either, same reason: they exist
# so a local `godot --export-release` needs no 1.2 GB template download, and a
# pointer is exactly what makes that impossible (all four are committed as
# 133-byte pointers today — see docs/FINAL_REPORT_2026-10-20.md, which could
# not unpack them). They are also what the web-preview job stages and pushes
# on every run, and an LFS-filtered path is the one thing in that step that
# needs git-lfs *and* a working LFS upload at push time.
engine/web_templates/*.zip -filter -diff -merge

# The web preview payload is deliberately NOT under LFS.
#
# It was, once, and it broke the thing it existed for: `web/index.wasm` and
# `web/index.pck` are what the browser loads, and a plain `git clone` fetches
# LFS *pointers* instead (133 bytes of text), so the preview died at
# `CompileError: expected magic word 00 61 73 6d`. Two things make pointers
# fatal here rather than merely inconvenient:
#   * CI checks out with actions/checkout@v4 and no `lfs: true`, so the job
#     that runs tools/web_qa.mjs against web/index.html got the pointer too;
#   * there is no git-lfs in this sandbox at all, and with `filter=lfs` set,
#     `git add` on these files fails outright ("external filter 'git-lfs
#     clean' failed").
# Yes, the pack is 35 MB and CI regenerates it. It stays in the tree because
# the preview has to work from a bare clone; if the churn ever matters the
# fix is to stop committing it and publish the CI artifact, not to hide it
# behind a filter that makes the repository un-runnable.

# Source art: 42 MB of rigged GLB and the Blender file, moved out of the
# repository root into source-assets/ during the phase-0 cleanup.
source-assets/**/*.glb filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
source-assets/**/*.blend filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Evidence and inspection images: 35 MB under docs/, 15 MB under qa-evidence/.
# Records, never compiled or loaded by anything.
docs/asset-inspections/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
docs/asset-inspections/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
docs/ui-redesign/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
qa-evidence/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
qa-evidence/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
exports/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
